### FastAPI Backend Implementation

First, let's create a FastAPI backend to handle API requests for blog posts. Create a new file called `main.py` and add the following code:

```python
from fastapi import FastAPI, Response
from pydantic import BaseModel
from typing import List

app = FastAPI()

class BlogPost(BaseModel):
    id: int
    title: str
    content: str

# Sample in-memory data store for blog posts
blog_posts = [
    BlogPost(id=1, title="Post 1", content="Content of Post 1"),
    BlogPost(id=2, title="Post 2", content="Content of Post 2"),
    BlogPost(id=3, title="Post 3", content="Content of Post 3"),
]

@app.get("/blog-posts", response_model=List[BlogPost])
def get_all_blog_posts():
    return blog_posts

@app.get("/blog-posts/{post_id}", response_model=BlogPost)
def get_blog_post(post_id: int):
    post = next((post for post in blog_posts if post.id == post_id), None)
    if post is None:
        return Response(status_code=404)
    return post

@app.get("/search-blog-posts")
def search_blog_posts(query: str):
    return [post for post in blog_posts if query.lower() in post.title.lower() or query.lower() in post.content.lower()]
```

